SUMMARY:Kagemusha | Michael A. McRobbie's Choice
DESCRIPTION:Akira Kurosawa's lauded feudal epic follows the story of a pe
 tty thief recruited to impersonate an aging warlord in an effort to keep 
 the warlord safe from attacking competing clans. When the warlord dies\, 
 his general reluctantly empowers the imposter to take over as the ruler t
 o maintain their control. But his commitment to his new role is tested wh
 en forced to lead "his" troops into battle. Winner of the 1980 Cannes Fil
 m Festival Palme d'Or\, Kagemusha merges the passion of youthful artistic
  creation with the genius of a master filmmaker. [162 min\; drama\, war\;
  Japanese with English subtitles]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Akira Kurosawa's lauded feudal epic fol
 lows the story of a petty thief recruited to impersonate an aging warlord
  in an effort to keep the warlord safe from attacking competing clans. Wh
 en the warlord dies\, his general reluctantly empowers the imposter to ta
 ke over as the ruler to maintain their control. But his commitment to his
  new role is tested when forced to lead "his" troops into battle. Winner 
 of the 1980 Cannes Film Festival Palme d'Or\, <i>Kagemusha</i> merges the
  passion of youthful artistic creation with the genius of a master filmma
 ker. [162 min\; drama\, war\; Japanese with English subtitles]</p>
