X-SOURCE:IU Cinema
DTSTART:20261028T180000Z
DTEND:20261028T190000Z
LOCATION:Zoom
SUMMARY:IU Cinema Creative Collaborations Zoom Q&A + Prep Session
DESCRIPTION:Registrants for this Q&amp\;A + prep session will be able to 
 speak with IU Cinema staff members regarding any questions related to the
  Creative Collaborations application process.  Creative Collaborations en
 ables groups at IU and in our community to highlight important topics and
  ideas through film screenings and film-related educational programs with
  a mission of:Fostering diverse programming partnerships that help bridge
  campus and community  Highlighting critical issues and themes through fi
 lm-related and educational programs curated in collaboration with IU Cine
 ma and subject-matter experts  Welcoming new and returning audiences to I
 U Cinema    Creative Collaborations is a competitive application process\
 , and any IU Bloomington unit\, student group\, Greater-Bloomington commu
 nity groups or non-profit organization is welcome to apply. Explore some 
 of our previous Creative Collaborations programming (https://cinema.india
 na.edu/about/partnerships/creative-collaborations-past-programming.html) 
 to get an idea of what past partners have presented.Applications for 2027
 –28 program proposals will be accepted from October 8–November 20\, 2
 026.  Full program guidelines are available at go.iu.edu/creativecollabor
 ations (https://cinema.indiana.edu/about/partnerships/creative-collaborat
 ions.html). You can register here (https://iu.zoom.us/meeting/register/Wr
 70_5MHT_OO4ZCtlu6ufQ) for this Zoom Q&amp\;A and prep session!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Registrants for this Q&amp\;A + prep se
 ssion will be able to speak with IU Cinema staff members regarding any qu
 estions related to the Creative Collaborations application process.</p><p
 >  Creative Collaborations enables groups at IU and in our community to h
 ighlight important topics and ideas through film screenings and film-rela
 ted educational programs with a mission of:</p><ul><li>Fostering diverse 
 programming partnerships that help bridge campus and community  </li><li>
 Highlighting critical issues and themes through film-related and educatio
 nal programs curated in collaboration with IU Cinema and subject-matter e
 xperts  </li><li>Welcoming new and returning audiences to IU Cinema  </li
 ></ul><p>  Creative Collaborations is a competitive application process\,
  and any IU Bloomington unit\, student group\, Greater-Bloomington commun
 ity groups or non-profit organization is welcome to apply. Explore some o
 f our <a href="https://cinema.indiana.edu/about/partnerships/creative-col
 laborations-past-programming.html">previous Creative Collaborations progr
 amming</a> to get an idea of what past partners have presented.</p><p><st
 rong>Applications for 2027–28 program proposals will be accepted from O
 ctober 8–November 20\, 2026.</strong></p><p>  Full program guidelines a
 re available at <a href="https://cinema.indiana.edu/about/partnerships/cr
 eative-collaborations.html">go.iu.edu/creativecollaborations</a>. You can
  <a href="https://iu.zoom.us/meeting/register/Wr70_5MHT_OO4ZCtlu6ufQ">reg
 ister here</a> for this Zoom Q&amp\;A and prep session!</p>
